# Web MVP Design Skills (Required)

When creating or redesigning **any website, landing page, dashboard, app UI, or frontend MVP**, read and follow the installed Agent Skills before writing UI code.

## Always do first

1. Read `web-mvp-design` skill (`~/.agents/skills/web-mvp-design/SKILL.md`) for the orchestration workflow
2. For new projects, run `setup` + `frontend-design` before implementation
3. Pick skills by task — do not skip the design stack for speed

## Skill map

| Task | Skills to read |
|------|----------------|
| Visual design & typography | `frontend-design`, `ui-design` |
| UI directions / less generic output | `add-ui`, `polish` |
| shadcn/ui components | `shadcn` |
| Design tokens & themes | `tailwind-design-system`, `design-system-patterns` |
| React architecture & performance | `vercel-react-best-practices`, `vercel-composition-patterns` |
| Animations & micro-interactions | `motion-foundations`, `motion-patterns`, `ui-animation`, `animate`, `interaction-design`, `css-motion-systems` |
| Accessibility & UX audit | `web-design-guidelines`, `ui-design` |

## MVP quality bar

- Distinctive visual identity (avoid generic AI aesthetics)
- Strong hierarchy, spacing, and typography
- shadcn/ui + Tailwind with semantic design tokens
- Purposeful motion with `prefers-reduced-motion` support
- Responsive, dark-mode capable, WCAG AA accessible
